{"id":"lambda","corpus":"aws","title":"AWS Lambda","sourceUrl":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/welcome.html","license":"AWS Documentation © Amazon Web Services, Inc.","blocks":[{"kind":"h1","text":"AWS Lambda"},{"kind":"p","text":"AWS Lambda is a serverless compute service. With Lambda, you can run code without provisioning or managing servers. Lambda automatically manages the underlying infrastructure – including server maintenance, capacity provisioning, scaling, and patching – so you can focus on your application logic."},{"kind":"p","text":"Lambda provides two compute primitives, each designed for different workload patterns:"},{"kind":"li","text":"Lambda Functions – Run code in response to events or API calls without managing servers. You write a handler function, connect it to a trigger (API Gateway, Amazon S3, Amazon SQS, EventBridge, and 200+ other AWS services), and Lambda executes it. Each invocation runs independently with no shared state, scaling horizontally to match demand. Lambda manages execution environments, scaling, routing, and fault tolerance."},{"kind":"li","text":"Lambda MicroVMs – Isolated compute environments with near-instant startup and state retention for up to 8 hours. Designed for workloads needing a dedicated compute environment for each individual user or job. Lambda manages isolation, capacity, and networking. Your application uses Lambda MicroVMs APIs and HTTPS endpoints to connect each user/job to their compute environment."},{"kind":"p","text":"For pricing information, see AWS Lambda Pricing."},{"kind":"h2","text":"How Lambda Functions and Lambda MicroVMs compare"},{"kind":"p","text":"Lambda Functions and Lambda MicroVMs share a common serverless foundation:"},{"kind":"li","text":"No server management – AWS manages underlying infrastructure, instance patching, and capacity."},{"kind":"li","text":"Pay-per-use billing – No upfront commitments. You pay only for the resources used."},{"kind":"li","text":"Managed networking – Both provide service-managed inbound and outbound network access."},{"kind":"li","text":"Firecracker virtualization – VM-level isolation between workloads."},{"kind":"p","text":"While they share this foundation, they serve different use cases:"}],"lemmas":{"lambdas":["lambda","lambdas"],"serverlesses":["serverlesses","serverless"],"computes":["computes","compute"],"computing":["computing","compute"],"computed":["computed","compute"],"serviced":["serviced","service"],"servicing":["servicing","service"],"running":["running","run"],"ran":["ran","run"],"codes":["code","codes"],"withouts":["withouts","without"],"provisioning":["provisioning","provision"],"provisionings":["provisionings","provisioning"],"provisions":["provision","provisions"],"provisioned":["provisioned","provision"],"managing":["managing","manage"],"managings":["managings","managing"],"servers":["server","servers"],"automaticallies":["automaticallies","automatically"],"manages":["manages","manage"],"underlying":["underlying","underlie"],"underlyings":["underlyings","underlying"],"underlies":["underlies","underlie","underly"],"infrastructures":["infrastructure","infrastructures"],"including":["including","include"],"includings":["includings","including"],"includes":["includes","include"],"included":["included","include"],"maintenances":["maintenance","maintenances"],"capacities":["capacity","capacities"],"scaling":["scaling","scale"],"scalings":["scaling","scalings"],"scales":["scale","scales"],"scaled":["scaled","scale"],"patching":["patching","patch"],"patchings":["patching","patchings"],"patches":["patch","patches"],"patched":["patched","patch"],"sos":["sos","so"],"foci":["focus","foci"],"focused":["focused","focus"],"focusing":["focusing","focus"],"focuses":["focus","focuses"],"applications":["application","applications"],"logics":["logic","logics"],"provides":["provides","provide"],"provided":["provided","provide"],"providing":["providing","provide"],"twos":["two","twos"],"primitives":["primitiv